    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 82\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 1848, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the public service law, in relation to requiring\n      corporations and municipalities to notify property owners prior to\n      beginning certain services\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require utilities to provide notice  to  customers  of\nany  non-emergency  work  which  the  utility  reasonably  believes will\ndirectly and materially impact the use of  residential,  commercial,  or\nother  property,  not  more than 30 days in advance of the start of such\nwork.\n \n  While I agree with the goal of this bill to ensure  notification,  the\nprovisions  of this bill present challenges for implementation and could\nimpede utility work that is necessary to maintain  the  reliability  and\nsafety  of New York's energy distribution systems. The ambiguity in this\nbill allows for misinterpretation by utilities and customers and,  at  a\nminimum,  would  likely  create  inefficiencies and delays in completing\nscheduled work. Lastly, any cost increases to utilities from this bill's\nambiguous requirements could be passed on to ratepayers, which is  unac-\nceptable.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 82,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2025
   }
